predef: "mixa_manager/mixa_audio_mp3.h.lm1"

# Header unit for the clean L2 port of mixa_audio_mp3 (ticket 20260913-
# 232000/231500 Part 2, module 5 of 8: the MP3 composition -- scan a
# directory, then launch the panel over what was found; the two-call
# glue joining mixa_audio_scan and mixa_audio_launch). Predefs the real
# header directly, unmodified, the same way the real mixa_audio_mp3.lm1
# already does (which itself predefs mixa_audio_scan.h.lm1 and mixa_
# audio_launch.h.lm1, unchanged either way). Total distinct predef'd
# files: 1 (transitively several more, none touched).
#
# NOTE ON THE ORACLE SIDE (stated here since it governs this whole
# module's parity gate): the real mixa_audio_mp3.lm1 needs 22 imports in
# one translation unit -- stable65D5's import path table caps at 16, so
# the STABLE pinned compiler cannot translate the real .lm1 at all. This
# was already solved once, by an earlier Claude session, in ticket
# 20260912-084943: Codex's own CANDIDATE compiler (SHA256 24A1B57B...
# 290B09, at build/codex/l1-import-capacity/build/import_capacity/
# run_20260912_084844/l1trans.exe) removes the cap and is used ONLY for
# this module's own oracle-side translation, exactly as run_mp3_
# selftest.ps1 already does -- read-only, hash-verified against the
# published value, with stable65D5's own hash independently re-verified
# unchanged on every run. This is not a new exception invented for this
# ticket; it is the same accepted precedent, reused.
